<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	NOVA currently declares no entitlements.

	`aps-environment: production` was removed here before the first App Store
	submission. It was dead: there is no `firebase_messaging` dependency, no
	`FirebaseMessaging` / `registerForRemoteNotifications` call anywhere in `lib/`,
	and no push-handling code in the Runner target — nothing ever obtained a device
	token, so the entitlement only asserted a capability the app does not use.

	It was not merely inert, either. `aps-environment` makes the App ID require the
	Push Notifications capability, so the provisioning profile has to carry it, and a
	profile generated without it fails to sign the archive. Removing the key lets the
	app be signed with an ordinary distribution profile.

	To add push later: re-add the key here, add `firebase_messaging`, register for
	remote notifications, restore the `remote-notification` background mode in
	Info.plist (also required for silent pushes), and enable the Push Notifications
	capability on the App ID in the Apple Developer portal.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
